Slippi's HTTP services (patches/net-0008), as Slippi Dolphin 3.7.0 and melee-unlocked use them:
- Display name refresh: after sign-in the netplay object asks Slippi's user service for the account's display name, connect
  code, latest version and chat messages (Slippi Dolphin's overwriteFromServer, melee-unlocked's User::RefreshFromServer), on a
  thread of its own; user.json is never written, and a failed request keeps what user.json says. Never with a local peer.
- Replay upload: when the game report's reply carries uploadUrl, the replay is asked for on the reporter's thread then
  (slippi::last_replay_path), not on the game thread when the game reports, so a host still writing it can finish first.
- Test builds name a loopback stand-in for these and the sign-in screen's requests (SLIPPI_PIN_SERVICES_URL; the Linux services build sets
  http://127.0.0.1:8766, ../tools/mock_slippi_http.py), so a development machine cannot reach the real ones.
The report's disc MD5 (isoHash, cached in iso_md5_cache.txt) is this repository's reporter as before.
Applied by ../net_sources.sh after net-0007. port/ is unchanged.

